// =============================================================================
// Detection: Sign-in from a blocked / high-risk country
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   Any sign-in attempt whose geo-IP country is on the organisation's BLOCK
//   list (enforced by CA004, a Conditional Access policy backed by a "blocked
//   countries" named location) or on the SOC's WATCH list (CA does not block
//   it). Every row gets an Outcome. CA is enforced only AFTER first-factor
//   authentication completes, so a wrong password never reaches CA
//   (ConditionalAccessStatus "notApplied"). Those rows are spray noise, which
//   failed-signin-spike.kql covers. They are NOT a CA gap. The thing to
//   investigate is Outcome == "SUCCEEDED - CA gap": a SUCCESSFUL sign-in from
//   a BLOCK-list country (a policy gap, an excluded app, report-only mode).
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   SigninLogs  (Microsoft Entra ID -> Diagnostic settings -> Log Analytics).
//   Geo comes from LocationDetails.countryOrRegion (falls back to the Location
//   country code). Outcome comes from ConditionalAccessStatus + ResultType;
//   the blocking policy names come from the ConditionalAccessPolicies array.
//
// LICENSE
//   - SigninLogs export requires Microsoft Entra ID P1 (or P2).
//   - Conditional Access (named locations, country block) requires Entra ID P1.
//   - Runs as a Log Analytics scheduled query or a Microsoft Sentinel rule.
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Travelling staff / VPN exit nodes in a blocked region trigger legitimately;
//     correlate with the user's normal pattern or a travel allow-list.
//   - Geo-IP is approximate; border/datacenter IPs can misattribute country.
//   - Keep BlockList in sync with the CA named location — drift here is a
//     silent gap. Consider sourcing both from one Sentinel watchlist.
//   - A spray from a listed country yields many "Failed first factor" rows.
//     Triage by Outcome, not by row count.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   As deployed by lab/terraform/modules/monitoring: Frequency 5m · Lookback
//   1h · Trigger > 0 rows · fixed Medium severity · Entities: Account=UPN,
//   IP=IPAddress. Suggested tuning (not deployed): raise severity ONLY when
//   Outcome == "SUCCEEDED - CA gap", not on Blocked == false.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE (Logic App - lab/monitoring/playbook-notify.json)
//   Shared by all five rules, Sentinel path only (the post-trial Log
//   Analytics alerts just email the ag-identity-secops action group).
//   Incident created -> automation rule (lab/terraform/modules/monitoring) ->
//   (1) Teams adaptive card: incident severity, title, number, created time,
//       status, description and an "Open in Sentinel" link;
//   (2) ServiceNow incident: urgency/impact from severity (Medium -> 2),
//       category "inquiry"; (3) the INC number is commented back on the
//       Sentinel incident for the audit trail.
//   NOT BUILT (production follow-up): on Outcome == "SUCCEEDED - CA gap", an
//   approval-gated Graph revokeSignInSessions (manual equivalent:
//   lab/scripts/powershell/04-Leaver.ps1).
// =============================================================================

// ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes. Keep in lockstep with the CA "blocked countries"
// named location. verify against your tenant's actual list.
// BLOCK list must match lab/terraform/envs/dev/lab.tfvars blocked_countries.
// WATCH list: CA does not block these, but the SOC wants eyes on them. The
// ListType column shows which list each hit came from.
let BlockList = dynamic(["KP","IR","SY","CU"]);
let WatchList = dynamic(["RU","CN"]);
// Codes where the FIRST factor failed, so CA was never evaluated:
// 50126 invalid username/password · 50034 user not found · 50053 locked
// (smart lockout) or malicious IP · 50056 no password on record · 50057
// account disabled. Any other failure (e.g. 50074/50076 MFA interrupt, 50055
// expired password) may mean the password was right -> review, not noise.
// verify: codes against the Entra AADSTS error-code reference for your tenant.
let FirstFactorFailures = dynamic(["50126","50034","50053","50056","50057"]);
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| extend Country = coalesce(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion), Location)
| where Country in~ (BlockList) or Country in~ (WatchList)
// Which CA policies (if any) returned "failure" (= blocked) for this sign-in.
// mv-apply with an inner summarize ALWAYS returns one row, so a sign-in that
// slipped through (no blocking policy) is kept, with BlockingPolicies == [].
| mv-apply CAP = ConditionalAccessPolicies on (
      where tostring(CAP.result) == "failure"
      | summarize BlockingPolicies = make_set(tostring(CAP.displayName))
  )
| extend ListType = iff(Country in~ (BlockList), "block", "watch")
// Blocked = CA itself stopped the sign-in. Blocked == false alone is NOT a gap:
// a wrong password is rejected before CA runs. Outcome tells them apart.
| extend Blocked = ConditionalAccessStatus == "failure"
| extend Outcome = case(
      Blocked, "Blocked by CA",
      ResultType == "0" and ListType == "block", "SUCCEEDED - CA gap",
      ResultType == "0", "Succeeded - watch list",
      ResultType in (FirstFactorFailures), "Failed first factor - CA not reached",
      "Other failure - review (password may be valid)")
| project TimeGenerated, UserPrincipalName, UserDisplayName, Country, ListType,
          IPAddress, AppDisplayName, Outcome, Blocked, ConditionalAccessStatus,
          BlockingPolicies, ResultType, ResultDescription, RiskLevelDuringSignIn
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
